      "explanation": "The view class only enforces authentication via IsAuthenticated but does not perform any role‑based permission checks for the bulk role management operation. The PUT endpoint allows a user to assign or revoke instructor/staff roles for any user after only verifying that the requester is authenticated, relying on internal checks that may be bypassed (e.g., missing explicit permission class for role management). This constitutes missing authorization for a protected operation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "lms/djangoapps/support/rest_api/v1/views.py",
          "lines": [34, 35],
          "content": "permission_classes = (IsAuthenticated,)\nserializer_class = CourseTeamManageSerializer"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "lms/djangoapps/support/rest_api/v1/views.py",
          "lines": [221, 238],
          "content": "def put(self, request, *args, **kwargs):\n    ...\n    auth_user = request.user\n    accessible_orgs, accessible_courses, user, validation_error = (\n        self._validate_permissions_and_user(auth_user, email)\n    )\n    ...\n    for operation_data in bulk_role_operations:\n        result = self._handle_role_assignment_entry(\n            operation_data,\n            auth_user,\n            accessible_orgs,\n            accessible_courses,\n            user,\n            course_key_cache,\n        )"
        },
